														<div class="brfprofile">
															<p class=""><b>Brief Profile:</b> With over 12 years of
																teaching experience, Shweta Rex is a seasoned
																English educator known for her dynamic classroom
																presence and creative
																approach to learning. She holds a Master’s degree in
																English from Jesus
																and Mary College, along with a B.Ed in English and
																Social Science, and
																is CTET-qualified. <br><br>
																Throughout her career, she has taught at renowned
																institutions such as St.
																Francis School, Father Agnel School, St. Paul’s School,
																The British
																School and Oxford Public School—each role strengthening
																her expertise
																in lesson planning, student engagement and event
																coordination. She has
																also contributed as a student counsellor at Career
																Launcher, guiding
																learners through academic support and personal
																development strategies. <br><br>
																Shweta is skilled in communication, people management
																and digital tools
																including MS Office and G Suite. She has successfully
																completed an
																FDP at IIM Rohtak on Case Study–Based Teaching Pedagogy,
																Case
																Preparation, and Effective Teaching through GenAI,
																further enriching her
																professional capabilities. <br><br>
																Her passion for music, reading and public speaking
																complements her
																commitment to nurturing confident, expressive and
																articulate learners.
															</p>
