													<div id="Button4" class="tabcontent">
														<h3 class="factitle">Innovative Teaching Methodologies for PGDM
															Students</h3>

														<p class="facpara">
															Training PGDM students to become well-groomed professionals
															required a practical and student-centric teaching approach
															rather than relying solely on traditional lectures. The
															methodologies used during the sessions focused on enhancing
															communication skills, confidence, leadership abilities,
															professional etiquette, and workplace readiness. These
															innovative approaches made the learning process more
															interactive, engaging, and aligned with corporate
															expectations.
														</p>

														<ul class="facul">

															<li>
																<strong>Experiential Learning Methodology:</strong>
																Experiential learning was widely used to ensure that
																students learnt through practical exposure and
																participation. Activities such as mock interviews, group
																discussions, presentations, and business communication
																exercises enabled students to experience real corporate
																situations. For example, students participated in
																simulated interview rounds where they were assessed on
																confidence, communication, and grooming. This
																methodology helped students gain hands-on experience and
																improved their overall professional presence.
															</li>

															<li>
																<strong>Role Play and Simulation-Based
																	Learning:</strong>
																Role plays and simulations were conducted to familiarise
																students with workplace behaviour and professional
																etiquette. Students enacted scenarios such as handling
																difficult clients, resolving workplace conflicts, and
																conducting team meetings. For instance, some students
																acted as HR managers conducting appraisal discussions.
																These activities improved communication skills, body
																language, confidence, and decision-making abilities
																whilst making the sessions more engaging and realistic.
															</li>

															<li>
																<strong>Activity-Based Communication Training:</strong>
																Communication training was strengthened through
																activities such as extempore speaking, JAM (Just A
																Minute) sessions, debates, storytelling, and
																presentations. Students were encouraged to speak on
																current and management-related topics to improve fluency
																and spontaneity. For example, students delivered short
																speeches on leadership, ethics, and workplace
																professionalism. Such activities gradually reduced stage
																fear and enhanced their confidence in formal
																communication settings.
															</li>

															<li>
																<strong>Peer Learning and Collaborative
																	Activities:</strong>
																Collaborative learning methods were adopted through
																group projects, brainstorming sessions, and team-based
																assignments. Students worked together on business
																pitches and management case discussions, which improved
																teamwork, interpersonal relationships, and leadership
																qualities. Peer learning also enabled students to learn
																from different viewpoints and communication styles,
																thereby creating a more inclusive and interactive
																classroom environment.
															</li>

															<li>
																<strong>Industry-Oriented Case Study Method:</strong>
																Real-life corporate case studies were incorporated to
																bridge the gap between theoretical learning and industry
																practices. Students analysed business situations related
																to leadership challenges, workplace communication gaps,
																customer handling, and ethical dilemmas. For example,
																discussions were conducted on cases where poor
																communication affected organisational reputation. This
																methodology developed analytical thinking,
																problem-solving abilities, and managerial
																decision-making skills.
															</li>

															<li>
																<strong>Reflective Learning and
																	Self-Assessment:</strong>
																Reflective learning encouraged students to identify
																their strengths and areas requiring improvement.
																Activities such as self-introduction recordings,
																personality assessments, and feedback discussions helped
																students become more self-aware. For instance, students
																reviewed recordings of their presentations to observe
																posture, eye contact, and speaking style. This
																methodology promoted continuous self-improvement and
																helped students consciously work on their professional
																image.
															</li>

															<li>
																<strong>Technology-Enabled Interactive
																	Learning:</strong>
																Digital tools and technology-based activities were
																integrated into the sessions to make learning more
																relevant to modern workplace requirements. Students
																created professional LinkedIn profiles, participated in
																virtual interview practice, and used presentation tools
																for business pitching exercises. Video-based learning
																and online communication activities also helped students
																understand the importance of digital professionalism and
																virtual communication in corporate settings.
															</li>

															<li>
																<strong>Mentorship and Coaching Methodology:</strong>
																A mentorship-based approach was adopted to provide
																personalised guidance regarding confidence building,
																interview preparation, communication skills, and
																workplace etiquette. Many students initially hesitated
																to participate in discussions or public speaking
																activities. Through regular mentoring, motivation, and
																constructive feedback, they gradually became more
																confident and expressive. This methodology created a
																supportive learning environment that contributed
																significantly to students’ personality development.
															</li>

															<li>
																<strong>Corporate Exposure and Industry
																	Interaction:</strong>
																Industry interaction sessions such as guest lectures,
																alumni talks, and corporate discussions exposed students
																to real workplace expectations. Professionals shared
																practical insights regarding leadership, workplace
																culture, interview etiquette, and professional conduct.
																These interactions gave students a clearer understanding
																of industry standards and motivated them to develop a
																more professional outlook towards their careers.
															</li>

															<li>
																<strong>Feedback-Oriented Continuous
																	Improvement:</strong>
																Continuous feedback remained an essential component
																throughout the training process. Constructive feedback
																was provided after presentations, mock interviews, and
																communication activities to help students identify areas
																for improvement. Guidance was offered on aspects such as
																confidence, voice modulation, professional dressing, and
																content delivery. This methodology encouraged students
																to refine their skills and become more polished
																professionals consistently.
															</li>

														</ul>

